                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Even while I have to merit the improvements of the Smash Edition of Super Comboman, I can sadly only verdict it be be less worse than the original release due to non-changing flaws and issues:\n\nThe pseudo-cellshading look looks exceptionally dodgy and low budget and is incapable of hitting the \"comic sticker vibe\" it is aiming for. Character design is very unique, but in this particular case \"unique\" in a devastatingly bad way. The entire game is full of cliche characters which don't feel comical or satirical at all and which I could imagine many people potentially being able to take offense with.\n\nWhat also didn't change is the fact that for a freeflow-button-mashing-combat-combo game the controls are actually too wonky to actually get into any kind of flow. Responsiveness of actions taken is sub-par, level design most of the time more frustrating than clever and I'm not even going to get started on the story, which should actually have been left out entirely and would have made this a better game altogether.\n\nI also have to add that I did receive the Smash Edition as part of a free upgrade due to owning the original game, but it is one of the games I could have totally done without. The 24 hours it took me to complete this could have been spent a lot better. Sure, even with all its flaws, the game is somewhat bearable, but there's no way I'd recommend it to anyone.",
